Verification note: Public documentation confirms the underlying CyberArk frameworks and drive-mapping feature. There is no confirmed turnkey Quantum Metric connector, tested DOM mapping, vendor-supported password API, or production proof that key injection and downloads work in this particular tenant. Those remain explicit POC deliverables.
Appendix A — Design discovery questionnaire
•	What is the exact Quantum Metric login URL and are local usernames/passwords allowed instead of mandatory SSO?
•	What is the approved local-account password change process or API contract?
•	What is the private-key input element type and Save confirmation behavior?
•	Does the input accept multiline PEM text; is the key ever shown after Save?
•	Does browser storage persist key material across sessions or shared-account users?
•	Are concurrent logins allowed and is there a maximum session limit?
•	What audit fields are available for decryption and export events?
•	Does Quantum Metric permit the proposed shared-account use under security policy and licensing?
